    {
      "fileName": "slam-down.json",
      "id": "39CqlOzlHjEhh0E4",
      "name": "Slam Down",
      "img": "icons/sundries/books/book-red-exclamation.webp",
      "type": "feat",
      "data": {
        "_id": "39CqlOzlHjEhh0E4",
        "folder": "EfAhkeT2DBo6O7NS",
        "img": "icons/sundries/books/book-red-exclamation.webp",
        "name": "Slam Down",
        "system": {
          "actionType": {
            "value": "action"
          },
          "actions": {
            "value": 2
          },
          "category": "class",
          "description": {
            "value": "<p>You make an attack to knock a foe off balance, then follow up immediately with a sweep to topple them. Make a melee Strike. If it hits and deals damage, you can attempt an Athletics check to [[/act trip]] the creature you hit. If you're wielding a two-handed melee weapon, you can ignore Trip's requirement that you have a hand free. Both attacks count toward your multiple attack penalty, but the penalty doesn't increase until after you've made both of them.</p>"
          },
          "level": {
            "value": 4
          },
          "prerequisites": {
